# Testing and Launch

Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: M4 Public release complete; native acceptance and hosting-policy risk remain
Dependencies: 01_PRODUCT_DECISIONS.todo, 05_WEBSITE_AND_ORDERING.todo

## Purpose

Keep technical checks, visual review, user approval and publication distinct.
Workstream 11 records the corrected palette/font and successful public release.
Workstream 09 preserves the sticker/source checks. Native acceptance and provider
commercial-use compliance are not established by publication.

## Tasks

- [x] Review keyboard navigation, visible focus, key contrast pairs and reduced motion.
- [ ] Complete native screen-reader and real-device acceptance.
- [x] Review small-phone/tablet/desktop layouts, simulated slower connection and no-JS fallback.
- [x] Verify at least 16px key text, principal 48px controls and 200% text resizing.
- [x] Verify the earlier three-section/no-form/five-cake revision; retain its evidence.
- [x] Verify home -> story -> cakes -> order, exact story/note restoration, full
  transparent stickers and full-JPG enlargement through workstream 09.
- [x] Record new build/Node/Python/browser results and actual visual inspection in 09.
- [x] Review the later cursive design, real font loading and 200% phone text in 10.
- [x] Exercise Instagram handoffs in the browser and synthetic WhatsApp URLs in Node.
- [ ] Confirm native Instagram/WhatsApp handoff after actual contact details are supplied.
- [x] Confirm no fake order-success/availability state or unintentional form submission.
- [x] Add titles, descriptions, headings, alt text and a generated sharing image.
- [x] Set the real public URL and confirm the deployed sharing image is reachable.
- [ ] Confirm actual social-app preview rendering.
- [ ] Check local business metadata against approved public information.
- [ ] Confirm photo permissions and remove sensitive metadata from public derivatives.
- [x] Exclude raw exports, private manifests, source screenshots, reference images and PDF.
- [x] Check actual responsive image loading, dimensions, crops and a cold slower connection.
- [ ] Confirm a suitable host's current terms and approved deployment configuration.
- [x] Release only when explicitly requested; inspect the actual deployed result.
- [x] Provide a prototype content/contact/photo maintenance guide.
- [ ] Record user acceptance without inferring it from generated artifacts.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] The public directory contains only intended customer-facing assets and font licenses.
- [x] Verify the current 66-file allowlist and exclusion of sticker
  manifests/masks/recipes, source README files and private model/review data.
- [x] There is evidence for the actual pages and links, not only a successful build.
- [x] Record the user's explicit launch authorization.
- [ ] Complete remaining business facts without inventing them.
- [x] GitHub source control is not confused with approval to host orders on GitHub Pages.

## Completion evidence

- Historical three-section result: 19 Node tests passed. That site was reviewed in headless Edge at
  320/390/600/768/1024/1440px, with no horizontal overflow or page-script errors.
- Visible mobile navigation, skip link, 30 sequential keyboard-focus steps, modal
  navigation/focus restoration, intercepted direct-contact handoffs, no-JS fallback
  and public-root exclusions exercised. Its main DOM text was 115 words (guard: 180);
  CSS-generated photo labels are separate from that count.
- Simulated cold load: 150ms latency and 200,000 bytes/sec download throughput.
- That prior evidence is retained under
  ..\.local\revisions\before-stickers-20261004\review\.
- Current result fields: 12_WHISK_AND_CRUMBS_BRAND.todo. npm test passed 25 cases;
  npm run build produced 66 files and brand-asset unittests passed four cases.
  Workstream 09 retains the five passing
  sticker/source-fidelity cases; the cursive revision does not change those assets.
- Current browser output: ..\.local\website-review\review.json reports passed,
  home/story/cakes/order, 188 main words (113 focus + 75 story), six transparent
  image instances with full-JPG viewer links and six tested widths. Labels are
  16px+ and controls 48px+; keyboard/dialog, no-JS, 200% text and slow-network
  coverage passed. The report has no timestamp field; final evidence was supplied
  by the parent on 2026-10-04.
- Parent visually inspected the final cream/dark contact sheet, desktop/mobile
  full pages and 200% order screenshot. Opaque source RGB equality and unchanged
  archived screenshot/crop hashes were included in the five sticker cases.
- No external message was sent. Real devices, native assistive technology and
  final user acceptance remain open.
- Importer testing belongs to 03_INSTAGRAM_IMPORT.todo and does not certify the site.

